  "description": "UQEDIH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C118 H136 Cl2 Co6 Dy4 N14 O36,8(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.164-3.867 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.37-113.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co6Dy4(HL)4(pdmH)2(pdm)8Cl2]·8H2O (C118H152Cl2Co6Dy4N14O44; Mr = 3545.02; CCDC formula C118H136Cl2Co6Dy4N14O36·8(H2O)). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
